I find Gauntlets of Dexterity to be essentially useless. Dexterity is 
easy to exercise, and the Gauntlets don't improve spellcasting success. 
I guess they're supposed to help with attack spells hitting their 
targets, but I've never noticed any discernable difference between 
well-exercised natural dexterity (should be 17 or 18 by the time you hit 
the Castle) and the bonuses GoDex can give you above that. Advanced 
players seldom miss in any event.

It would be nice if GoDex were more like GoPower: automatic 25 
dexterity, with some nice bonuses achievable at that level. They should 
help with spellcasting success as well, since it is the rigidity of 
metal armor that allegedly hinders spellcasting because it restricts the 
necessary movements.

